meta {
  name: 43 Set Grouping Mode (Group Settings)
  type: http
  seq: 43
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/tenant/accession-settings/grouping-mode
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "groupingMode": "DEPARTMENT_SAMPLE_NAME"
  }
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("echoes the saved grouping mode", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().data).to.have.property("groupingMode");
  });
}

docs {
  Change the Accession **Group Settings** mode that **new orders** take
  (`AccessionGroupingMode`). Business-admin only (`ACC_SETTINGS_UPDATE`).

  **Not retroactive.** Every order carries its **own** mode (`orders.grouping_mode`),
  decided once, when the order first gets samples, from the tenant mode at that
  moment, and never changed afterwards (a database rule refuses any change). So
  this call only affects orders that get their samples later: existing orders keep
  the grouping their barcodes were made under, and **no barcode is ever cleared,
  renumbered or regrouped by this call** (barcodes are on printed labels, in
  transfers and matched by the lab analyzers). An order that has no mode yet
  (a draft / quote / appointment with no samples) follows the tenant's current
  mode until its first sample is made.

  One transaction: the tenant row is locked first (so the "old mode" is the true
  predecessor even when two admins save at once, and an order created at the same
  moment sees either entirely the old or entirely the new mode), the mode is
  saved, and the audit row is written in the same transaction. A save of the mode
  the tenant already has changes and records nothing.

  **Busy (409 `TENANT_GROUPING_MODE_BUSY`).** If another request (an order being
  created, another admin saving) keeps the tenant row locked for more than 3
  seconds, this call gives up with a 409 instead of hanging. Nothing was changed
  and nothing was recorded; the admin can simply save again.

  **Audit:** one `TENANT` / `UPDATE` audit row per real change, with
  `metadata: { oldMode, newMode }` and a description "Changed the Accession Group
  Settings grouping mode from X to Y (applies to new orders only)". It is written
  by the service in the same transaction (not after the response), so a change can
  never be saved without its record.

  `groupingMode` — one of `SAMPLE_NAME` | `ORDER` | `DEPARTMENT` |
  `DEPARTMENT_SAMPLE_NAME`.
}
